From 21f7adafb641677ce2e7a96b2937bc992ee3d486 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Calogero Mandracchia <calogero@efebia.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:18:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] process-status-file: a status file for each interactive
 process

From the TUI's first screen until it exits,
$CODEX_HOME/processes/<pid>.json tells which conversation the process
shows, its working directory and terminal pane, and whether a turn is
running in it, with the field names other tools already read: pid,
procStart, sessionId, cwd, tmux, status, kind, version, startedAt,
updatedAt and statusUpdatedAt. sessionId is null on the startup
screens, which show no conversation yet.

The file is written atomically (a temporary file in the same directory,
then a rename) with private permissions, only when something changes,
and removed by a guard when the TUI exits. procStart, field 22 of
/proc/<pid>/stat, tells a reused pid from the original process. Files
left by processes that were killed are removed by the next start, on a
background thread that also asks tmux for the pane's location.

CODEX_PROCESS_STATUS_FILE=0 (or false, off, no) turns it off. Errors
are ignored: the file is a hint for other programs and never stops
Codex.
